@echo off
rem Fun e2e: a headless agent play-tests Bloxorz (turn-based block-rolling puzzle), records a video,
rem and either makes real progress or bails early with a diagnosis. NO fullscreen workaround.
call "%~dp0run-mcp.cmd" "Using ONLY the windows-computer-use MCP tools (do not use Bash): open a web browser to https://www.coolmathgames.com/0-bloxorz and play Bloxorz - roll the 1x2 block with the ARROW KEYS into the square hole. Click through ads/menus/tutorial into Stage 1. KEY TECHNIQUE for browser games: left_click ONCE directly on the game board/canvas to give it focus (act auto-routes keys to the browser via window-messages), THEN send arrow keys; focus persists until you click elsewhere, so you do NOT need to re-click before every key. Do NOT use the game's fullscreen mode. Verify each move actually happened by checking the on-screen Moves counter (it should increment) - if it does not increment, your click missed the canvas, so screenshot, re-click the board precisely, and retry. Use the record tool to capture a short video clip (~6-8s) while making moves so there is an mp4 to review. Make at least 5-6 real moves toward the hole. Report whether keyboard input worked (did Moves increment?), what you saw on the board, and the exact mp4 path."
